      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The present study evaluates whether the closing procedure of the femoral artery after percutaneous coronary intervention influences the degree of inflammation related to the procedure as measured by C-reactive protein (CRP) and serum amyloid A (SAA). A thrombin-based device (Duett sealing device) was compared with a mechanical compression device (FemoStop)."},
